CHIP-8
======

This program is derived from the CHIP-8 machine in Time Warp Studio
(https://github.com/James-HoneyBadger/Time_Warp_Studio), which is MIT licensed.

Where the behaviour, the constants and the words came from:

  Time Warp Studio                                  This repository
  ------------------------------------------------- -----------------------------
  native/src/lang/chip8.cpp                         chip8/machine.py
      the Chip8Machine: opcodes, quirks, fonts          (behaviour ported 1:1)
  native/include/timewarp/lang/chip8.hpp            chip8/machine.py
      constants, Chip8State, the machine's interface    (constants.py)
  native/src/lang/chip8.cpp (assemble_chip8)        chip8/assembler.py
      the two-pass assembler and the ROM loader
  native/src/ui/chip8_emulator.cpp                  chip8/emulator.py
      Chip8Emulator: frames, speed, rewind
  native/src/ui/chip8_screen.cpp                    chip8/frontend_terminal.py
      keypad mapping, colours                           chip8/frontend_x11.py
  docs/chip8/README.md                              README.md
  docs/chip8/instruction-set.md                     docs/instruction-set.md
  docs/chip8/assembly.md                            docs/assembly.md
  Examples/chip8/*.ch8                              examples/*.ch8 (copied)
  docs/chip8/README.md (the machine's behaviour)     docs/instruction-set.md

New in this repository, and not from Time Warp Studio:

  chip8/lib/*.inc            the standard library: text, draw, math, input,
                             and the 4x5 ASCII font that tools/make_font.py
                             generates
  roms/*.ch8                 hello, clock, life, plot, snake
  chip8/assembler.py         the linker: data section, .include/LIB, .org,
                             .print/.printc, _hi/_lo/_len names
  chip8/frontend_terminal.py the terminal frontend
  chip8/frontend_x11.py      the X11 frontend (libX11 through ctypes)
  chip8/screen.py            the framebuffer renderer
  chip8/inspector.py         the text inspector
  chip8/librarian.py         the program catalogue and the `new` template
  chip8/cli.py               run, library, new, dev, asm, info
  roms/, tests/, tools/
